<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results on Simpler-WidowX.</span> We report the success rates (%) of various VLAs fine-tuned on the Bridgev2 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Walke et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. For <math id="S3.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Black et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, <math id="S3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-FAST <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pertsch et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and GR00T N1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">GEAR, 2025</a>)</cite>, we report the performance by fine-tuning the pre-trained model with the official implementations,
and other reported numbers borrow from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qu et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
