<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="S3.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Component-wise analysis</span> on Libero <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023a</a>)</cite> and Simpler-WidowX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> benchmarks. All models are <math id="S3.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Black et al., 2024</a>)</cite> fine-tuned for 60K iterations with a batch size of 32, using the Libero training dataset for Libero and the BridgeV2 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ebert et al., 2021</a>)</cite> for Simpler-WidowX. We report the averaged success rates (%) of the models on each benchmark.</figcaption>
</figure>
            
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center">
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:230.5pt;height:93.1pt;vertical-align:-45.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-81.5pt,32.9pt) scale(0.6,0.6) ;">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:393.5pt;height:158.8pt;vertical-align:-76.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
